# --- supersession notes (D0106 ruling 2; D0128) ------------------------------
# tests/laws/m1/test_l1_rel.py
#   RETIRED, ONE node: test_l1_5_mixing_semirings_is_refused_by_name.
#   Its line 244 builds `Rel(("a",), [({"a": 1}, (2, Why.zero))])` as incidental
#   filler, and D0110 (owner-authorised) makes an unwitnessed nonzero annotation
#   unconstructible. The file stays frozen and unedited; the node's claim — mixing
#   semirings is refused by name — is carried forward verbatim by L2.2 in
#   tests/laws/m2/test_l2_sources.py. The entry is in governance/laws.yaml, and M2
#   Session B moved it from `pending` to `superseded` in the same change that landed
#   D0110 — so conftest.py now marks it xfail(strict=True) and it must FAIL, which it
#   does. Every other law in that file is unaffected and stands.
#
#   (The Session A spelling of this note named `governance/superseded-laws.yaml`, a
#   file that has never existed; the registry has been `governance/laws.yaml`
#   throughout. Corrected here rather than left to mislead — D0135.)
